  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/... \nWith strong dry air advection in place behind the departing \ntrough, weather conditions will turn much quieter beginning on \nFriday. A piece of energy left behind from departing trough is \ncurrently being depicted by the model guidance to separate itself \nfrom the main jet energy and briefly morph into a cut-off low over\nAZ during the weekend. This feature for the most part should be \ninconsequential, although enough moisture could be present for \nsome showers to materialize over the AZ high terrain on Saturday \nbut for the most part should remain on the light side given the \noverall lack of instability that will be present. The lower \ndeserts should remain rain-free as there will be too much dry air \nin place. Under the presence of the low, temperatures will be \nseveral degrees below normal during the weekend with afternoon \nhighs struggling to reach 80 degrees across the lower deserts. As \nthe upper-level low exits the region and weak ridging builds \noverhead early next week, temperatures will rebound to more \nseasonal levels.",
